F10 is at corrected_v4/v3_guards.py:189, reached by prepare_review_bundle.py:157 and root_native_runtime_read_probe.py:40. The socket expression `(?m)^\s*(?:http_unix_socket):\s*\S` lets the post-colon whitespace consume a newline and its next non-whitespace token match the next ordinary field key. Thus `http_unix_socket:` with an empty inline value can appear populated. Root's actual clean-runtime probe PID 41795 exited 1 at 08:02:00 UTC before creating the probe directory, before any account/PR/remote service read and before native preparation. Exact failure stderr is 1460 bytes/SHA256 4c03ccbef208e6c338d28c4ed944ece54a054f55e4b77d8e25201d6acf831620. Root's metadata-only diagnosis PID 42500 at 08:03:04 UTC binds unchanged config.yml 824 bytes/SHA256 8c09fd1cf968d4e2e5456aea12041795a2764269aa4eb867cb0391e51887d94f, empty actual inline value, socket match beginning line 13 spanning two lines, and no external-alias match. I authenticated that receipt/stream custody and read its metadata, not the real private body.

